package com.astro.prediction;

import java.util.Map;

public final class NakshatraTexts {
    private NakshatraTexts() {}

    public static String get(String name) {
        return DATA.getOrDefault(name, "Born under " + name + ", you carry the unique signature of this lunar mansion through every area of your life.");
    }

    static final Map<String, String> DATA = Map.ofEntries(
        Map.entry("Ashwini", "Ruled by Ketu, governed by the twin divine physicians, Ashwini blesses you with healing instincts, athletic vitality, and the pioneer's drive to begin. You initiate effortlessly and recover from setbacks faster than most. The shadow is impulsiveness — speed without reflection leaves important things unfinished. Career alignment: medicine, athletics, emergency services, veterinary work. Spiritually, Ketu's past-life wisdom gives you flashes of sudden insight. Your soul purpose is learning to apply speed with precision — beginning with clear intention and completing with sustained dedication."),
        Map.entry("Bharani", "Ruled by Venus, governed by Yama the lord of dharma and endings, Bharani holds the tension between creation and destruction, pleasure and responsibility. You feel at extraordinary depth — love, grief, and passion move through you with a creative force that others rarely access. The shadow is holding on beyond a relationship's natural season. Career alignment: creative arts, psychology, law, obstetrics. Spiritually, Yama's domain of right endings invites you to work consciously with the universal cycle of release — what you grieve completely, you eventually transcend."),
        Map.entry("Krittika", "Ruled by the Sun, governed by Agni the purifying fire, Krittika gives you a razor-sharp discernment, natural authority, and a directness that cuts through pretence without apology. You say what you see, and you see more clearly than most. The shadow is harshness — the critical faculty turned inward or wielded without compassion. Career alignment: surgery, military leadership, editorial work, teaching. Spiritually, Agni's fire is the sacred flame of honest transformation; your path involves refining yourself and your world through the courageous practice of truthful illumination."),
        Map.entry("Rohini", "Ruled by the Moon in its own exaltation nakshatra, governed by Brahma the creator, Rohini is one of the most creatively gifted and materially abundant placements in the entire system. You possess magnetic beauty, artistic brilliance, and a natural capacity to attract resources, relationships, and beauty into your orbit. The shadow is attachment — holding comfort, people, and pleasures beyond their season. Career alignment: arts, music, fashion, luxury goods, agriculture. Spiritually, Brahma's creative power invites you to recognize your gifts as a sacred endowment to be shared generously."),
        Map.entry("Mrigashira", "Ruled by Mars, governed by Soma the moon-nectar deity, Mrigashira creates the eternal seeker — gentle, curious, restless, always following a scent toward something beautiful just beyond the current horizon. Your mind is genuinely multi-disciplinary, finding pleasure in the exploration itself as much as in any destination. The shadow is the deer's flight — from commitment, depth, and the discomfort of fully arriving. Career alignment: research, linguistics, travel, writing, marketing. Spiritually, the search outside is ultimately a journey inward — the beauty you seek is the aware presence within you."),
        Map.entry("Ardra", "Ruled by Rahu, governed by Rudra the storm-Shiva, Ardra brings intensity, intellectual brilliance, and transformative disruption. Early suffering often functions as an initiatory furnace that forges extraordinary depth of insight and compassion. Your analytical mind cuts through complexity with precision. The shadow is the storm's destructive aspect — restlessness that disrupts what needs only adjustment. Career alignment: advanced research, technology, physics, psychology, investigation. Spiritually, Rudra's dissolution asks you to trust that what breaks in your life breaks to make room for something essential."),
        Map.entry("Punarvasu", "Ruled by Jupiter, governed by Aditi the goddess of boundless possibility, Punarvasu carries the energy of renewal — light returning after darkness, second chances that redeem difficult beginnings. You are genuinely optimistic and resilient; setbacks are temporary phenomena to you rather than permanent verdicts. Career alignment: teaching, philosophy, counseling, travel, international work. Spiritually, Aditi — the infinite — reminds you that there are no irrecoverable failures. Your soul purpose is demonstrating to others that light reliably returns, that renewal is always available."),
        Map.entry("Pushya", "Ruled by Saturn in its most auspicious expression, governed by Brihaspati the teacher of gods, Pushya is traditionally the most universally favorable nakshatra. You are the nourisher — steady, trustworthy, quietly devoted to the well-being of those in your care. Saturn's structure here becomes patient wisdom rather than mere restriction. Career alignment: education, social work, community leadership, traditional medicine, finance. Spiritually, the teaching is that true nourishment flows from inner abundance — you cannot give sustainably from depletion. Self-care is a sacred act."),
        Map.entry("Ashlesha", "Ruled by Mercury, governed by the Naga serpent deities of hidden wisdom and kundalini, Ashlesha gives you a penetrating psychological intelligence that perceives the hidden currents beneath visible behavior with uncanny accuracy. Hypnotic presence, strategic thinking, and access to deep intuitive knowing are genuine gifts. The shadow is the serpent's sting — sharp words or manipulative moves when direct expression feels unsafe. Career alignment: psychology, research, healing arts, strategic fields, occult sciences. Spiritually, the Nagas' kundalini energy points toward the conscious raising of primal instinct into enlightened awareness."),
        Map.entry("Magha", "Ruled by Ketu, governed by the Pitris — ancestral spirits carrying collective lineage wisdom — Magha gives you a natural aristocratic bearing, deep pride in heritage, and an instinctive connection to the authority of those who came before you. Leadership comes naturally; people accord you respect before you have formally claimed it. The shadow is attachment to status as a substitute for inner worth. Career alignment: government, history, ceremony, cultural preservation, institutional leadership. Spiritually, your task is to honor what was noble in your lineage while consciously releasing what was limiting."),
        Map.entry("Purva Phalguni", "Ruled by Venus, governed by Bhaga the god of good fortune and marital happiness, Purva Phalguni creates the natural enjoyer and generous giver of life's pleasures. You possess social magnetism, creative flair, and an infectious warmth that elevates any environment you inhabit. Joy is something you generate and transmit. The shadow is comfort-seeking that avoids necessary difficulty. Career alignment: performing arts, music, fashion, event management, entertainment, counseling. Spiritually, Bhaga teaches that conscious pleasure, freely shared, is itself a devotional act."),
        Map.entry("Uttara Phalguni", "Ruled by the Sun, governed by Aryaman the deity of righteous covenants and patronage, Uttara Phalguni creates the dependable covenant-keeper whose word is their bond and whose commitments form the bedrock of their identity. Generosity and sustained kindness mark your relationships. Career alignment: law, medicine, social work, diplomacy, management. The shadow is carrying excessive responsibility and struggling to ask for reciprocal support. Spiritually, Aryaman's domain of right relationship extends to your relationship with the divine — your path involves fulfilling your soul's agreements with full, conscious grace."),
        Map.entry("Hasta", "Ruled by the Moon, governed by Savitr the life-giving Sun, Hasta blesses you with extraordinary practical intelligence, multiple skillful gifts, and a dry humor that navigates social complexity with lightness. Your hands, mind, and organizational ability work in concert to produce results others find remarkable. Career alignment: healing arts involving hands, writing, teaching, craftsmanship, astrology. The Moon's rulership introduces emotional cycles that require conscious management. Spiritually, Savitr's creative power flows through your skilled work — every craft you master is a form of reverence for the sacred creative force."),
        Map.entry("Chitra", "Ruled by Mars, governed by Vishvakarma the divine architect, Chitra creates the master creator driven by the pursuit of breathtaking quality, visual harmony, and perfect design. You see the divine proportions underlying aesthetic experience and refuse to accept the mediocre. Career alignment: architecture, jewelry, fashion, film, fine arts, surgery. The shadow is perfectionism — satisfaction perpetually postponed because nothing yet meets the impossible standard. Spiritually, Vishvakarma's craftsmanship invites you to regard your entire life as your ongoing masterwork — each relationship and choice a brushstroke in a sacred ongoing creation."),
        Map.entry("Swati", "Ruled by Rahu, governed by Vayu the wind god of freedom and breath, Swati creates the flexible free spirit — socially gifted, diplomatically skilled, and drawn instinctively to wide open spaces of possibility. Like the young plant shoot bending in the wind, you survive through adaptability rather than rigidity. Career alignment: trade, diplomacy, social media, travel, yoga teaching. Rahu amplifies appetite for novelty and foreign influences. The shadow is dispersal across too many interests. Spiritually, Vayu's breath connects you to the life force itself — your path is to be pervasive but purposeful, free but not formless."),
        Map.entry("Vishakha", "Ruled by Jupiter, governed jointly by Indra and Agni — divine authority and purifying fire — Vishakha creates the purposeful achiever whose focused intensity, once directed, is formidable and ultimately triumphant. You often stand at significant crossroads, and your choices carry exceptional consequence. Career alignment: law, leadership, science, competitive athletics, activism. The shadow is obsession — the same focused energy that drives achievement can become an unhealthy fixation. Spiritually, the twin deities invite you to bring both human competence and divine fire to your highest purpose — to pursue it with complete dedication."),
        Map.entry("Anuradha", "Ruled by Saturn, governed by Mitra the god of friendship and covenantal love, Anuradha creates the devoted friend and loyal networker whose depth of commitment and warmth of community build enduring bonds across remarkably diverse circles. Struggle followed by breakthrough is a recurring life pattern — hence the name 'subsequent success.' Career alignment: diplomacy, counseling, organizational leadership, foreign affairs, research. The shadow involves intensity that can tip into possessiveness. Spiritually, Mitra's covenant extends toward the divine — your deepest allegiance is ultimately to your own soul's authentic path."),
        Map.entry("Jyeshtha", "Ruled by Mercury, governed by Indra the champion of cosmic right order, Jyeshtha creates the protector who steps forward when others retreat — bearing the weight of authority not for glory but because someone must. You are placed in elder or leadership roles earlier than might seem appropriate. Mental sharpness and strategic intelligence are exceptional. Career alignment: government, law, protective services, crisis management, organizational leadership. The shadow is the burden of perpetual responsibility — difficulty asking for help or showing vulnerability. Spiritually, Indra's battle against opposition reminds you that the greatest conflict is ultimately with your own limiting beliefs."),
        Map.entry("Mula", "Ruled by Ketu, governed by Nirriti the goddess of dissolution and root causes, Mula creates the compulsive root-seeker — one who must go all the way to the bottom of every phenomenon, every relationship, every belief to find the truth that actually matters. You are drawn to edges, depths, and places where conventional wisdom does not reach. Career alignment: pure research, root-cause medicine, philosophy, investigation, ancient knowledge systems. Ketu's influence brings sudden spiritual insight alongside radical disruption. Spiritually, Nirriti's dissolution is liberation — your path clears the ground of everything inauthentic for the truest version of your existence."),
        Map.entry("Purva Ashadha", "Ruled by Venus, governed by Apas the cosmic waters of purification and irresistible flow, Purva Ashadha creates the invincible visionary — one whose words, creative output, or philosophical conviction reshape the landscape of their world with the patient, unstoppable force of a great river. Once you commit to a direction, you are formidable. Career alignment: philosophy, writing, law, politics, teaching, the arts. The shadow is pride in conviction — difficulty revising your position once stated. Spiritually, Apas teaches that the true victory is over the obstacles within yourself — the pride and rigidity that prevent the free flow of your highest nature."),
        Map.entry("Uttara Ashadha", "Ruled by the Sun, governed by the ten Vishvadevas representing collective virtues, Uttara Ashadha creates the universal dharmic whose victories serve not just themselves but the entire network of life around them. Your integrity is extraordinary — your word means something even when honoring it is costly. Career alignment: government, military leadership, institutional management, education, medicine. The shadow is inflexibility — the conviction of rightness that resists genuinely alternative perspectives. Spiritually, the ten Vishvadevas represent completeness of character — your path involves the gradual integration of all virtues: courage, generosity, honesty, and grace."),
        Map.entry("Shravana", "Ruled by the Moon, governed by Vishnu the all-pervading preserver, Shravana creates the sacred listener — one who receives knowledge with unusual depth, integrates it thoroughly, and transmits it with the clarity of someone who has truly heard. You are often extraordinarily learned, not merely informed. Career alignment: teaching, music, journalism, counseling, linguistics, archiving. The Moon's rulership gives strong emotional intelligence and intuitive grasp of subtle communication. The shadow is absorbing others' realities so completely your own perspective becomes obscured. Spiritually, the deepest listening is to the voice of the divine within all things."),
        Map.entry("Dhanishtha", "Ruled by Mars, governed by the eight Vasus — elemental deities of abundance and cosmic rhythm — Dhanishtha creates the prosperous rhythmist who achieves excellence through disciplined energy and a natural sensitivity to timing. Music and rhythm are often deeply important. Career alignment: music, athletics, real estate, engineering, organizational management. Mars provides abundant drive and competitive courage. The shadow is a restlessness that makes inner stillness difficult — the drive to achieve crowds out the quiet depth that would ultimately enhance outer accomplishments. Spiritually, abundance shared with integrity is sacred participation in the universe's generative nature."),
        Map.entry("Shatabhisha", "Ruled by Rahu, governed by Varuna the deity of cosmic law and the mystical ocean depths, Shatabhisha creates the solitary healer who possesses extraordinary perceptual capacity and reserves of healing power — 'a hundred healers' — that must be developed largely through independent inner work. You prefer reaching your own conclusions through direct observation. Career alignment: alternative medicine, astrology, technology, environmental science, philosophy at the frontier of knowledge. The shadow is isolation — comfort in the inner world that delays necessary outer engagement. Spiritually, Varuna's cosmic waters invite you to become fluent in the invisible laws operating beneath the visible surface."),
        Map.entry("Purva Bhadrapada", "Ruled by Jupiter, governed by Aja Ekapada the lightning-fire of radical spiritual transformation, Purva Bhadrapada creates the spiritual warrior whose idealism burns with an intensity that both illuminates and sometimes scorches. Your depth of feeling and range of spiritual longing are among the most intense in the zodiac. Career alignment: spiritual teaching, depth psychology, mystical arts, transformational healing, philosophy. Jupiter's breadth is transformed here from comfortable wisdom into urgent revelation. The shadow involves extremism — the fire of spiritual intensity flipping into zealotry or excessive austerity. Spiritually, Aja Ekapada's lightning points toward sudden, direct awakening — recognition of your true nature beyond all conditioning."),
        Map.entry("Uttara Bhadrapada", "Ruled by Saturn, governed by Ahir Budhnya the primordial serpent dwelling in the cosmic depths, Uttara Bhadrapada creates one of the most profoundly wise and quietly powerful presences in the entire nakshatra cycle. A settled inner depth, earned through genuine inner work, makes you feel ancient even in youth. Career alignment: spiritual teaching, social service, depth psychology, medicine, academia where accumulated wisdom defines contribution. Saturn brings extraordinary patience and willingness to do unglamorous inner labor. Spiritually, the primordial serpent connects you to the deepest stratum of consciousness, where individual identity dissolves into universal awareness — the most complete of all paths."),
        Map.entry("Revati", "Ruled by Mercury at the zodiac's completion point, governed by Pushan the guide of souls through every threshold, Revati carries the accumulated wisdom of all twenty-six nakshatras before it — the compassion of completion, the readiness for renewal that only the truly finished can welcome. Your empathy functions as psychic perception; your compassion as a form of medicine. Career alignment: healing arts, music, counseling, social service, film, spiritual guidance, work involving safe passage through mystery. The shadow is sensitivity without adequate boundaries — absorbing too much from the world's ocean. Spiritually, your sacred function is to be a light at the crossing, helping others through what seems impassable.")
    );
}
